          "content": {
            "id": "c7e62c2d-5e5e-3893-a745-478c8182a018",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Fatburger Owner Faces Allegations It Masked Liquidity Crunch",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "The company, which owns Fatburger and Johnny Rockets, resorted to high-interest loans known as merchant cash advances as its finances deteriorated, according to a pair of complaints filed in Delaware Chancery Court since late November.  The shareholder accuses FAT Brands of misrepresenting debt as cash to try to win fresh financing.  The MCAs, together with other transactions that were \u201cdesigned to artificially inflate its cash position and disguise its liquidity issues,\u201d suggested deeper troubles with the firm\u2019s finances that weren\u2019t \u201cproperly accounted for in FAT\u2019s publicly disclosed financial statements or disclosed to investors,\u201d according to one of the complaints.",
